      "title": "Reference to Video (prompt)",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the character in <Picture 1>: describe the hair, outfit and any held items as seen in the reference.\n<Subject 2> is the setting: describe the background.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video is a 5-second, single-shot anime-style character clip. The character looks at the camera and speaks one short line.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - face, hairstyle, outfit and items are retained.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a clean, high-detail anime illustration brought to life, with crisp line art and soft lighting.\n[Shot 1] A medium shot (bust-up to knee-up framing works best with this workflow): <Subject 1> stands in front of <Subject 2>. Hair and clothes sway gently. The character smiles at the camera and says in Japanese, \"こんにちは。今日もよろしくね。\" The camera slowly pushes in.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSoft ambient room tone and the character's clear young voice.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nLight, gentle background music.\n",
